  "$notes": "Free-text explanations reproduced verbatim in data-report.md, so anyone reading the generated dataset can see why a value differs from the snapshot.",
  "notes": {
    "vatican-city": "The snapshot marks Vatican City as unMember: true. It is a UN permanent observer, not a member; corrected here, which brings the UN member count to the correct 193.",
    "hong-kong": "The snapshot gives the capital as 'City of Victoria', a historic name rather than a current capital. Hong Kong is an SAR and has no capital, so the capital list is emptied — which excludes it from capitals and combo questions through the pool filter, not through a hard-coded exclusion (§3.3, locked decision 4).",
    "palestine": "Ramallah is the de facto administrative seat and the primary answer; Jerusalem is listed as the declared capital and is accepted in expert mode. Inclusion is not a statement on sovereignty — see the About copy in Settings.",
    "western-sahara": "Disputed territory. El Aaiún is the largest city and the answer used; the Sahrawi Republic administers from Tifariti. Alias 'Laayoune' accepted.",
    "kosovo": "Uses the user-assigned ISO code XK, which is what flag-icons ships the flag under.",
    "eswatini": "The snapshot lists only Lobamba. Mbabane is the administrative capital and the primary answer; both are accepted.",
    "sri-lanka": "The snapshot lists only Colombo. Sri Jayawardenepura Kotte is the official capital and the primary answer; both are accepted.",
    "chile": "§5.2 names 'Chile/Texas-alikes' as a confusable pair, but Texas is not an entity in this dataset. Paired with Cuba instead, which is the closest genuine confusable in scope."
  },
